%%{init: {"theme": "neutral"}}%%
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant P as The page (markets.js)
  participant W as SQL engine (background worker)
  participant M as MEDUSA server
  participant K as Workers KV
  participant B as Binance
  P->>M: GET /api/session, is this session signed in?
  M-->>P: yes
  P->>P: draw the empty page
  P->>M: GET /api/market/metrics/mine
  P->>M: GET /api/market/scanner
  M->>K: read market/scanner.json
  K-->>M: about 160 KB, ready-made
  M-->>P: your definitions, the daily tables, the publish records
  par All at once, nothing waits for anything else
    P->>W: start SQLite (WebAssembly)
  and
    P->>B: open the live stream
  and
    P->>B: GET /ticker/price, every price once
  and
    P->>B: GET /exchangeInfo, each market's type (once a day)
  and
    P->>B: GET /klines per market, only while the lakehouse is behind
  end
  W-->>P: ready, empty tables
  B-->>P: prices, types, yesterday's closes
  P->>W: fill the tables, run the queries for the view on screen
  W-->>P: every number
  P->>P: draw them
  Note over P,B: From here on: the live loop, about once a second
